WEBVTT

NOTE map-navigation: written VO text from episode.json, timed from the timeline VO placements

V0-1
00:00:02.250 --> 00:00:05.266
Read the stations on the map,
move the moisture bands,

V0-2
00:00:05.366 --> 00:00:08.160
switch to variance, and
filter what the map shows.

V1a-1
00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:17.990
The map plots each sprinkler of a station
scanned in the past seven days at its own

V1a-2
00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:22.772
coordinates. A station scanned today is
filled with the color of the moisture band

V1a-3
00:00:22.872 --> 00:00:27.670
its reading falls into, and a station last
scanned on an earlier day is drawn clear.

V1b-1
00:00:28.233 --> 00:00:32.249
Four bands by default:
0 to 5, 6 to 19, 20 to 30,

V1b-2
00:00:32.349 --> 00:00:37.923
and above 30 percent. The colors
and boundaries are yours to change.

V2a-1
00:00:44.543 --> 00:00:47.803
The color bar under the
legend has draggable handles.

V2a-2
00:00:47.903 --> 00:00:50.733
Move one and the map
recolors when you let go.

V2b-1
00:00:51.293 --> 00:00:55.073
Dragging a handle changes the boundary
and saves it to your preferences.

V3a-1
00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:05.930
The button beside the legend
toggles between VWC and variance.

V3b-1
00:01:06.413 --> 00:01:10.963
Variance colors each station by
how far it sits from its own target

V3b-2
00:01:11.063 --> 00:01:15.343
instead of by its raw reading:
three bands, centered on target.

V4a-1
00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:27.350
Layers chooses which stations are drawn:
all of them, or only the enabled ones.

V4b-1
00:01:27.816 --> 00:01:32.302
Disabled stations are not being adjusted,
so hiding them leaves only the stations

V4b-2
00:01:32.402 --> 00:01:36.446
your push will affect. Layers saves
your choice to your user preferences.

V5a-1
00:01:43.660 --> 00:01:47.086
Selecting a station in the
table highlights it on the map,

V5a-2
00:01:47.186 --> 00:01:50.200
and selecting a station on
the map selects the row.

V5b-1
00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:52.737
One selection, shown in both panels.

V5b-2
00:01:52.837 --> 00:01:55.750
Use whichever is faster to
find the station you mean.
